WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.524
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:09.164
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.464 --> 00:00:16.250
Unit twenty-seven: Past Simple (regular verbs). Today you will talk about finished actions in the past.

4
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.307
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.232
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:25.108
Yesterday.

7
00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:28.488
Yesterday means the day before today.

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:30.735
I played football yesterday.

9
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.188
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

10
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.081
Yesterday.

11
00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:39.609
Walked.

12
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:42.430
Walked means the past of walk.

13
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:44.354
She walked to school.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.138
Your turn. Say: Walked.

15
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:50.897
Walked.

16
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.384
Played.

17
00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:55.162
Played means the past of play.

18
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.448
They played all afternoon.

19
00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.540
Your turn. Say: Played.

20
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.169
Played.

21
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:05.767
Watched.

22
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:08.667
Watched means the past of watch.

23
00:01:09.283 --> 00:01:10.598
We watched a film.

24
00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:13.383
Your turn. Say: Watched.

25
00:01:16.233 --> 00:01:17.176
Watched.

26
00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:18.755
Studied.

27
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.703
Studied means the past of study.

28
00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:23.794
He studied English.

29
00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.583
Your turn. Say: Studied.

30
00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:30.400
Studied.

31
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.290
Last night.

32
00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:36.177
Last night means the evening or night before today.

33
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:38.702
I slept early last night.

34
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:42.608
Your turn. Say: Last night.

35
00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:46.642
Last night.

36
00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:48.199
Ago.

37
00:01:49.183 --> 00:01:51.589
Ago means back in the past from now.

38
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:53.707
I met her two years ago.

39
00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:56.737
Your turn. Say: Ago.

40
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.555
Ago.

41
00:02:01.317 --> 00:02:02.132
Finished.

42
00:02:03.117 --> 00:02:05.197
Finished means the past of finish.

43
00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:07.226
I finished my homework.

44
00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:10.097
Your turn. Say: Finished.

45
00:02:12.933 --> 00:02:13.725
Finished.

46
00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:18.091
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.950
Visal, what did you do yesterday?

48
00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:35.630
I played football and I studied English. We use the past simple for finished actions. For regular verbs, we add -ed: play, played; walk, walked; watch, watched.

49
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:38.414
Are there any spelling rules?

50
00:02:39.517 --> 00:02:54.223
If a verb ends in e, we add d: like, liked. If it ends in consonant + y, change y to ied: study, studied. Short verbs often double the last letter: stop, stopped.

51
00:02:55.317 --> 00:02:57.711
Does the past form change with he or she?

52
00:02:58.817 --> 00:03:08.890
No! It is the same for every subject: I played, she played, they played. Time words like yesterday, last night and two days ago help us.

53
00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.510
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:16.509
Grammar focus: Past simple: verb plus -ed.

55
00:03:16.809 --> 00:03:18.031
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.717 --> 00:03:20.658
I played football yesterday.

57
00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.364
She walked to school last week.

58
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.029
We watched a film last night.

59
00:03:26.967 --> 00:03:35.520
For finished actions in the past, add -ed to regular verbs. The form is the same for every subject. Spelling: e + d, y becomes ied.

60
00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:39.667
Be careful! Don't say: I playd football yesterday.

61
00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:43.981
Say: I played football yesterday.

62
00:03:44.281 --> 00:03:46.002
Add -ed to the base verb.

63
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.383
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:51.574
A Busy Yesterday.

65
00:03:51.874 --> 00:03:54.303
Yesterday I walked to school with my friends.

66
00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.195
We played football at lunch time.

67
00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.873
Last night I studied English for one hour.

68
00:04:01.867 --> 00:04:04.702
I watched a film with my family two hours ago.

69
00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.920
I finished my homework before I slept.

70
00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:13.093
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.752
I blank football yesterday.

72
00:04:16.052 --> 00:04:19.276
A, play. B, played. C, playing.

73
00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:24.612
The answer is B: played.

74
00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.657
She blank English last night.

75
00:04:27.957 --> 00:04:31.250
A, studied. B, studyed. C, studys.

76
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.440
The answer is A: studied.

77
00:04:37.583 --> 00:04:39.792
'Two days ago' is a blank time word.

78
00:04:40.092 --> 00:04:43.490
A, past. B, future. C, present.

79
00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:48.986
The answer is A: past.

80
00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.848
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:52.148 --> 00:04:57.879
A, He walkd to school.. B, He walked to school.. C, He walks to school yesterday..

82
00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:03.839
The answer is B: He walked to school..

83
00:05:04.983 --> 00:05:08.109
According to the reading, what did the writer do last night?

84
00:05:08.409 --> 00:05:13.073
A, studied English. B, played football. C, walked to school.

85
00:05:16.633 --> 00:05:19.016
The answer is A: studied English.

86
00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.201
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.655
What did you do yesterday?

88
00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.183
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:36.483 --> 00:05:53.420
Yesterday I walked to school and studied English. After lunch I played football with my friends. In the evening I watched TV with my family. All of these verbs end in -ed because they are regular verbs in the past simple.

90
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.708
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.617 --> 00:06:01.812
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past simple: verb plus -ed.

92
00:06:02.112 --> 00:06:06.099
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:09.469
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:12.607
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

